The final goal is a near-real-time debate analysis system capable of transforming spoken debate into structured and explainable analytical feedback.

BiasLess is designed as an assistive and explainable debate-analysis system. Its classifier outputs, decision-strength indicators, evidence signals, argument-quality scores, and counterarguments should be interpreted as analytical assistance rather than unquestionable judgments about a speaker, claim, or argument.